    {
      "id": "1h0dlwa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Rise of New Religions"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Jainism was founded by Rishabhdev (1st Tirthankara) and popularized by Vardhamana Mahavira (24th Tirthankara).",
        "The Three Jewels of Jainism (Triratna) consist of Right Faith, Right Knowledge, and Right Conduct.",
        "Buddhism was founded by Gautama Buddha, focusing on the Four Noble Truths and the Eightfold Path (Astangika Marga).",
        "Important scriptures include the Jain Agamas and the Buddhist Tripitakas (Sutta, Vinaya, and Abhidhamma Pitakas).",
        "Major sectarian splits led to Svetambara and Digambara in Jainism, and Hinayana and Mahayana in Buddhism."
      ],
      "id": "k6t1rg2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ncokz3c",
      "content": "• By the 6th century BCE many people were dissatisfied with the complex rituals of Vedic religion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8i5h0un",
      "content": "• The dominance of Brahmins and rigid caste system created social tensions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lukzrsb",
      "content": "• Expensive sacrifices (Yajnas) were difficult for common people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uirddyi",
      "content": "• As a result, new religious movements like Jainism and Buddhism emerged."
    },
    {
      "id": "akxzfzh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Jainism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "umi40p6",
      "content": "Jainism is one of the oldest religions in India. It emphasizes non‑violence, self‑discipline and spiritual purity."
    },
    {
